# probe_config_H10D.prb
# Cambridge NeuroTech ASSY-77-H10 (H10-D), 64 ch, 2 shanks x 32.
#
# Geometry     : probeinterface cambridgeneurotech/ASSY-77-H10 (authoritative)
# Pin order    : ASSY-77 H10-D-map.pdf
# Hardware map : H10_D_open_Cheetah2026-07-21_16-59-03.cfg
# Verified vs  : screen_details.txt (6 Cheetah display windows)
#
# Journey: probe pin --(+63)--> NLX AD ch --> CSCn --> CSCn.ncs
#          --> binary row n-1 --> Kilosort channel n-1
#
# y is HEIGHT ABOVE THE TIP (y=0 tip, y=330 topmost), matching
# probeinterface. This is flipped vs. the earlier revision of this file.
#
# Slot pitch 15 um. Each shank has 23 slots but only
# 22 contacts: slot(s) [21] (y=[15.0]) are empty, so
# each tip contact sits 30 um below its neighbour, not 15 um.
#
# All 64 channels resolve to a real contact. CSC32 (AD ch 60) does not
# decode via pin = hw-63, but is the back-shank tip (pin 48): AD ch 111
# is unused, pin 48 is the only unclaimed site, and the screen layout
# places CSC32 at the bottom of the back centre column. Not a bad channel.
#
# Groups are shanks: 0 = back (ch 0-31), 1 = front (ch 32-63).

